# Moss Docs

> Moss is a high-performance runtime for real-time semantic search. It delivers sub-10 ms lookups, instant index updates, and zero infra overhead. Moss runs where your agent lives - cloud, in-browser, or on-device - so search feels native and users never wait.

- [Docs](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/index.md)
- [What is Moss?](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/start/what-is-moss.md): Real-time semantic search that runs where your agent lives
- [Quickstart](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/start/quickstart.md): Install, authenticate, create an index, and query it (JS/Python tabs)
- [Core Concepts](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/start/core-concepts.md): Indexes, embeddings, retrieval, sessions, sync, and the rest of the Moss model.
- [Vibecoding with Moss](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/start/vibecoding.md): Starter prompts, LLM-friendly docs, and MCP setup for building Moss-powered apps with AI coding tools.
- [Real-Time Local Indexing](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/real-time-local-indexing.md): Index and query in-process with a local session - no per-operation network call.
- [Live-Call Context](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/live-call-context.md): Query a persistent cloud index and a live session together during a conversation.
- [Data Hydration & Sync](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/data-hydration-sync.md): Hydrate on-device indexes from the cloud and keep them fresh with zero-downtime hot-swaps.
- [Cross-Agent Context & Omni-Channel Handoff](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/cross-agent-handoff.md): Hand a conversation off across agents, channels, and devices with full context intact.
- [Sub-10ms Knowledge Retrieval](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/offline-first-search.md): Load an index into memory and run semantic queries in-process.
- [Voice Agent (LiveKit)](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/voice-agent-livekit.md): Ground a LiveKit voice agent in your Moss index for real-time retrieval.
- [Agent Context](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/agent-context.md): Persist and recall agent context as documents in a Moss index.
- [Browser Extension Context](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/browser-extension-context.md): Run indexing and queries in the browser with the @moss-dev/moss-web SDK.
- [Electron App Local Search](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/electron-local-search.md): Run a Moss index in the Electron main process and query it from the renderer over IPC.
- [Local Embeddings](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/build/local-embeddings.md): Embed documents on-device with a built-in model.
- [Authentication](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/authentication.md): Configure project credentials for the Moss SDKs
- [Indexing Data](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/indexing-data.md): Prepare and upsert your content into Moss indexes
- [Sessions](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/sessions.md): Local-first, real-time indexing with create-resume-query-push.
- [Retrieval](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/retrieval.md): Choose vector, keyword, or hybrid retrieval
- [Hybrid Search](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/hybrid-search.md): Blend semantic and keyword scoring with a single alpha parameter.
- [Metadata Filtering](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/metadata-filtering.md): Narrow query results to documents whose metadata matches a filter.
- [Custom Embeddings](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/custom-embeddings.md): Bring your own vectors instead of a built-in on-device model.
- [Multi-Index Search](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/multi-index-search.md): Search across multiple loaded indexes in one call and get a global top-K.
- [Storage & Persistence](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/storage-persistence.md): Persist loaded indexes to disk and keep them in sync with the cloud.
- [Deployment / Production](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/integrate/deployment-production.md): Checklist for shipping Moss-backed features
- [Errors & Troubleshooting](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/reference/errors.md): Reference for common Moss SDK errors and how to fix them
- [Pricing & Limits](https://docs.moss.dev/docs/pricing.md)
